{
    "description": "Shared fold-authority parity fixture. The Rust daemon (crates/daemon/src/config.rs) and the TypeScript plugin (packages/opencode-plugin/src/config/index.ts) load every row through their production loaders and must produce the same summarizer chain, admission, and Eidnara-folds predicate.",
    "contract": [
        "A row's user_tier_files are written to $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/eidnara and its project_tier_files to <project>/.eidnara; each key is a file name and each value is the file's text. env holds the only variables {env:} substitution may read.",
        "expected_chain is the ordered, deduplicated user-tier summarizer chain. expected_admission is admitted or unresolved. expected_eidnara_folds is an admitted configuration with compaction.enabled !== false and a non-empty chain. An unresolved row withholds its documents' chain, so expected_chain is null, and it leaves folding to the host's native compaction, so expected_eidnara_folds is false.",
        "Chain values are trimmed of ECMAScript whitespace (String.prototype.trim), which includes U+FEFF and excludes U+0085.",
        "Supported input, the limit parity is claimed for: every tier file is a regular UTF-8 file of at most 1 MiB (1,048,576 bytes) whose final path component is not a symlink, and the user tier is valid JSONC before variable substitution. The daemon reads each tier with O_NOFOLLOW and that bound and reports a larger or symlinked tier as unreadable; the plugin follows symlinks and reads any size.",
        "A malformed or non-object tier, a summarizer or compaction block the user tier does not hold as an object, an unknown key inside history_summarizer or compaction in either tier, a user-tier key holding a variable reference, a non-boolean compaction.enabled, and a mistyped chain key are unresolved on both sides. Known keys are the plugin schema's properties (assets/eidnara.schema.json). The plugin also rejects unknown keys outside those two blocks, while the daemon ignores them and reads its own keys the plugin schema lacks (for example memory.user_profile_budget_tokens), so keys outside those two blocks are outside the parity contract.",
        "The four chain keys (model, fallback_models, module_model, module_fallback_models) take literal model ids: a blank value or one containing {env: or {file: is excluded with a warning on both sides, while the rest of the document keeps the plugin's substitution. compaction.enabled must be a literal boolean."
    ],
